{{ opt }}
{% endfor %}
```
{% else %}
*None read — `start.sh` did not match the expected shape.*
{% endif %}

**Heap matches production exactly** (`-Xms2560m -Xmx5120m`). GC behaviour is
load-sensitive, so a different heap would make results untransferable.

Two options here are additions production does not have, both deliberate:
`spring.datasource.tomcat.max-active`, because the pool is unconfigured in
production and sits at the Tomcat JDBC default — the harness predicts that
default is itself the first choke point, so it has to be a knob rather than an
accident; and `logging.level.org.avni`, because `AuthenticationFilter` logs
twice per request including the full query string, which is a plausible
bottleneck in its own right.

